WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:07.060
A man takes one last sip of whiskey.  He gets in his car and drives to his favorite place,  Glenwood Canyon.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:13.960
He arrives, parks his car, takes out a flashlight and a car registration from the glove box and then unscrews his license plate.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.049
He throws his registration and license plate into the river as he walks to a particular spot

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.689
He and his wife would always spend time at when she was still alive

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:26.518
It's one of the highest points of the canyon and it has an incredible view of the valley beneath it

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.710
He has come to commit suicide

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:33.238
The man stands at the edge of the canyon thinking one last time about his life

00:00:33.489 --> 00:00:38.159
He looks out at the massive beautiful landscape the night sky sprinkled with stars

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:43.079
Seamlessly converges with the stone of the canyons edge as it trips down into the river beneath

00:00:43.149 --> 00:00:49.229
He feels a combination of wonder and pain as he's admiring the landscape a woman's voice behind him yells,

00:00:49.229 --> 00:00:55.619
Hey! Startled, the man almost falls, but then catches himself. He turns around to find a woman appearing out of the forest

00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:58.679
She wears a long dress and has long silvery straight hair

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.809
She's old, but sort of pretty. It's late and dark and the man wonders why she's here by herself.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:09.179
She approaches the man and says "Hello". Kind of confused and thrown off, the man says "Hello" back

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:13.650
"What are you doing here so late by yourself?" the man asks. In kind of a snarky way

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:17.900
The woman responds with the same question. "What are you doing here so late by yourself?"

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:22.739
Again thrown off the man says, "I don't know. I guess I just needed to clear my head."

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:24.100
"This is my favorite spot."

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.280
You're awfully close to the edge of that cliff to be clear in your head replies the woman are you going to jump?

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.680
No, like I said, I'm just here to clear my head. I've had a long couple of days says the man

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:38.670
Okay, well have a good night says the woman she begins to walk away

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.990
this confuses the man

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:41.979
He had quickly

00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:48.029
constructed a fantasy in his head that this woman was some deity type who appeared by fate to save him to convince him not to jump.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:53.909
To change his mind about life as the woman walks away, the man calls out. Hey wait!

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.699
You never said why you're here. The woman turns around

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.599
You never said why you're here replies the woman. Yes, I did

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.449
I just told you the man says with a nervous guilty laugh

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:08.339
The woman gets really close to the man quickly moving from where she was right up into the man's face

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.860
Why you're really here. She whispers.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:15.239
The man thrown off yet again stutters. I'm clearing my fucking head, okay!?

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:16.450
Why don't you believe me?

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:22.349
the woman turns around and begins to walk away again as she begins to walk further away the man panics at the thought of the

00:02:22.349 --> 00:02:28.048
woman leaving without trying to save him. He yells out. Okay, fine. I'm here to jump. The woman turns around

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:34.739
Pardon? She asks, I'm here to kill myself. This life is awful and I'm ready to die. Okay. There you go

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:38.908
The woman comes back to where the man standing. What's so awful about it?

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:44.249
She asks, what's not so awful about it? Replies the man. It's filled with ugliness and sadness

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:50.429
There's tragedy, there's conflict, there's heartbreak, It's endlessly difficult for no reason, success is hard

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.759
There's no obvious meaning to anything, even just the little things.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.709
The traffic, the cold weather, the Mondays, the way the grocery stores are lit, and the god-awful

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:02.009
cashiers that always look at you like they'd be better off if you weren't alive

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:09.358
Well, what life would you not want to jump from? Ask the woman. A life without all that obviously - says the man. A life filled

00:03:09.359 --> 00:03:12.569
With only beauty, happiness, love and peace.

00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:14.200
A life that's easy and fun all the time

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:19.380
One where there's apparent meaning to stuff and we actually know what's going on and why we're here and what the point is

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:27.260
One with no heartbreak, no tragedy. No conflict. No hardship. No mean grocery store cashiers, no traffic. No Monday's, no pain

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:33.760
Hmm. Says the woman. Everything would be perfect and I would never want to leave that life. Says the man

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.800
The man and the woman stare at each other for a second. It feels like a few.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.800
So who are you you? You have to tell me why you're here now. The man agitatedly asks again.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.900
The woman moves closer to him. I'm who you hoped I was.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:50.699
Confused the man backpedals a little bit completely forgetting where he's standing

00:03:50.699 --> 00:03:56.969
What do you mean? Asks the man. The woman leans in to answer and pushes the man softly on his chest.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.309
He falls backwards off the cliff

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.709
The man awakes in his bedroom, it's a normal Tuesday morning

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:11.439
He thinks about how horrible the nightmare he just had was. But like most dreams, he quickly forgets and moves on

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.480
He gets out of bed and gets ready. He gets dressed, eats breakfast and leaves his house

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:21.160
The sky is bright pink and purple with a sunny glow that illuminates the whole world

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:27.730
The grass is richly green and smells like the first spring to ever take place in the universe. The birds harmonized together perfectly

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:34.089
Every person is smiling cheek to cheek as if their faces are pinned in such a position. The man is entirely happy.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:39.880
He has no sense of sadness. Everything is beautiful with no sight of ugliness. The world has no conflict.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:45.339
Everyone loves each other equally. There's no heartbreak, no hardship. No bad days. No traffic,

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:52.540
No mean grocery store cashiers. Life is easy and smooth and fun. The meaning of life and the nature of reality is clear and everyone

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:57.000
knows exactly what's going on. It's completely and entirely perfect.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:03.609
A year or so goes by. The man is at home. He takes one last sip of water. He gets in his car and drives to Glandwyn Canyon

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.300
It's not too far from where he lives

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:11.169
He parks his car, takes out a flashlight and the car registration from the glove box and then unscrews his license plate

00:05:11.419 --> 00:05:15.609
He throws his registration and license plate into the river as he walks to a spot

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:19.150
That's one of the highest points of the canyon. He has come to commit suicide

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.379
He stands at the edge of the canyon thinking about his life one last time

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:27.580
He looks out at the massive beautiful landscape the night sky sprinkled with stars

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:33.609
Seamlessly converges with the stone of the canyons edge as it trips down into the river beneath. He feels nothing

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:36.909
He's about to jump when a woman's voice from behind him yells, Hey

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:42.669
Startled the man almost falls, but catches himself. He turns around to find a woman appearing out of the forest

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:49.450
This woman's presence is not interesting or perplexing to the man. She approaches the man and says hello and asks him what he's doing

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:55.989
I'm going to jump. Says the man. Why? asks the woman. It's a waste being alive, isn't it? There's nothing to do

00:05:56.030 --> 00:06:01.330
Everything is easy and boring I want to feel but there's nothing to feel answers the man

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.080
Well

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:08.739
What life would you not want to jump from? Asks the woman. A life that's interesting and exciting and actually has feeling obviously.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:12.099
Replies the man. Well, what makes a life that way? Asks The woman.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:18.400
I don't know, one where some stuff is beautiful, but not everything. Or perhaps everything is beautiful,

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.360
but at least you don't always notice it so you can actually appreciate it when you do

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:28.650
A life where you're happy some of the time, but not all the time, and some of the time you actually feel really sad, so you can tell the difference

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:32.000
One where everyone doesn't love each other and some people aren't really that nice at all

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.880
So you can actually feel special about certain people. When where bad stuff happens once in a while one where things are actually kind of hard,

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:44.340
and finding success and meaning requires some thought, effort, and creativity, so it actually feels important when you find it

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:48.020
One here nothing is ever perfect, but some stuff can get really close if you try hard enough.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:54.860
I never want to leave that life. Doesn't it sound wonderful? Asks the man. Yes. Says the woman. It does.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:59.839
The man turns around to look at the landscape over the cliff and try to imagine a life like that

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:06.200
The woman leans in and pushes him softly on the back. He falls forward off the cliff

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.829
Hope you see at this time. The woman says to herself

